  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between 7,2',6'-Trihydroxy-5-methoxyflavanone and HCC1937 through a series of target interactions involving SNU-387. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, all of which ultimately target HCC1937. The shared involvement of SNU-387 in these pathways indicates a potential mechanism by which 7,2',6'-Trihydroxy-5-methoxyflavanone may exert its effects on HCC1937. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of SNU-387, which in turn affects HCC1937. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the interaction between 7,2',6'-Trihydroxy-5-methoxyflavanone and HCC1937, reinforcing the possibility of a shared biological mechanism.",
